{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794258780,"nonce":"cYht3dnR4XHbssVXuBZ7e+IaQxk=","title":"VideoPlayer is never torn down","message":"From the allocation audit (code read; growth not observed in a running app).\n\nblinc_media video.rs: the player's tick callback is registered and never removed, and the player has no `Drop`. The callback holds the current frame (about 8 MB at 1080p) and, on desktop, the whole source file. Each player also mints five `use_state_keyed` signals under a monotonic id. On the web, web_video.rs keeps `WEB_VIDEOS` entries, their DOM elements and an unrevoked blob URL.","files":null}]}